[Music]  season six of Game of Thrones lives on  in our hearts but there are a few  characters that have long left the world  of the living  deaths are a huge part the Game of  Thrones experience some are expected  while some are not some ringers pain  while others bring us a kind of morbid  joy but over six seasons HBO sure have  got good at them these are the six best  deaths of Game of Thrones Season six  Episode one kicked off with a pretty  heavy death after the coup of dawn the  murder of Doran Martell and the  assassination of princess Marcella in  season five the sand snakes abara and I  Marius and ambushed the prints on his  barge as he busies himself painting some  pebbles while he gets to choose how he  dies he should have kept his wits about  him because unfortunately he's the first  gruesome death the season the tip of Oba  Haris spear exploding from the young  prince's face as he turns to face  Nymeria left to bleed on the floor as  the sisters swap their awkward banter on  the way out you're a greedy [ __ ] you  know that  we've been hoping these two traitors  bite the bullet ever since they muttered  as they plunge their knives deep into  our beloved John Snow well I'm sure they  didn't expect the young Lord Commander  to rise from the dead and hold them  accountable for their crimes that little  [ __ ] Olli thorn and the other traitors  are seen new stand ready to be hung by  the neck until dead now this may not be  that gruesome but you've got to hand it  to the makeup department for their  depiction of hanged man truly unsettling  out of all the deaths on this list this  is probably the one that was most  intense after learning of Hodos old self  before he became the simple giant that  Shepherds bran threw the unwelcome North  he suddenly snatched away from us during  his final noble deed saving bran from  one of his many bloody screw-ups  Hodor takes scratches and bites and  holds back a wave of the night Kings  undead army but he did his job he held  that door and now he holds our hearts  the Lord of the most northern house of  Westeros was adamant that he loved to  fight wildlings he's been doing it all  his life well if that's the case then  maybe he should have learned not to let  his guard down during the battle the  bastards it wasn't looking good to  Tommen even taking a few head butts once  the Warriors have become squashed  together but as soon as small Jon looks  towards the arriving Knights of the Vale  he gets a big old chunk bitten out his  throat then again I'm sure wildlings  have even worse Walder Frey was a  disgusting man so it's only right that  his last meal was as foul as he was  we've seen people get their throat cut  on the show before sure but we've never  seen a gross old man he a pie made from  the flesh of his two sons the mixture of  him slowly realizing the ingredients of  his pie the panic on his face as he  knows he's about to die and the look of  Glee on iies face as he bleeds out all  over himself and his dinner made many  viewers wince on the other hand he's a  horrible old codger who made the red  wedding happen so to hell with him  Ramsey's death was what we wanted for a  long time he's been the target of much  fan hatred and deservedly so of all the  evil characters are of all their evil  acts I think he's definitely top of the  rankings from chopping up sausage and  feeding newborn babies to dogs to  slaying anyone in his path this  despicable warden of the North seemed  untouchable and ultimately vile so  there's no surprise that each punch Jon  Snow delivered to that smug bastards  face fell  oh so good to watch and the beautiful  horrifying irony of having his own  bloodthirsty hounds rip him apart just  as he's done to so many others was  brutally satisfying I think we all felt  like Sansa in that moment it was tough  to watch but we just couldn't look away  so those are my picks for the six best  deaths of season six if you've got any  you think deserved a place on this list  then let us know in the comment section  below or tweet me at a regular Dave for  more Game of Thrones features make sure  you subscribe to GameSpot  [Music]

